#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Gapmer ASO Design: a third design strategy, ALLELE-SELECTIVE.

Picked, the design walks only the registers that sit OVER a mutation on the track and designs nowhere else,
so every ASO returned covers a changed base. Tiles are shared round-robin between the mutations, so a
maximum smaller than the full walk covers every mutation before covering any of them twice. "Design against
this track's alleles" is turned on and held there: an ASO built on the reference is complementary to the
other allele at the very base that distinguishes them.

    sudo python3 install-allele-selective-tiling.py /opt/baja-apps

Also fixes the coordinate bug that made the strategy unavailable: a variant's xi is in the track's own x,
which starts at track.xi, so on a genomic track every variant mapped past the end of the designed sequence.
"Design against this track's alleles" and "Avoid sites carrying variants on other tracks" were silently
doing nothing there for the same reason, and now work.

Writes baja/manchester/menu/design-mutation-sites.js and edits aso-design-dialog.js, track-design-menu.js,
design-scope-from-workbench.js and py/ssaso/design.py (each backed up as <file>.before-allele-tiling). Refuses, changing nothing, if a file
differs from the version this was made against. Safe to run twice.
"""
